        "payload": "tree 2d101fd90da0a3d66291363ae7d3cd79d125698a\nparent aa44a3a431a599e4ec07331e9f10e3cc34fc4049\nauthor Palash Bansal <palash@shaders.app> 1794507548 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1794507548 +0000\n\nplugin-cloud: a page without storage asks before it takes a key, naming the key's account\n\nA sandboxed page (files.threepipe.org) cannot keep the state of its own sign-in, so handleRedirect took any key in\nthe URL, and a link carrying someone else's key signed the visitor in to that account: their saves, shares and\nreports went there (found by the release review of 0.1.0-next.0). Such a page now asks first, with the email the key\nwas issued to, read from the key (a link can change tp_cloud_user, not that). `auth.confirmUnverified(account)`\nreplaces the confirm() dialog; where confirm() is not available, no sign-in. Pages with storage check the state as\nbefore and never ask.\n\nChecked in Chromium on a page served with the files.threepipe.org sandbox CSP: sessionStorage throws, the dialog\nnames the key's account and not tp_cloud_user, Cancel leaves the page signed out, OK signs in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWN5WJVoif5u2R5D96ps9b\n",
